dialect protocol
protocol stdio.gltf.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.gltf.mutations
start op

# P2-FG3: real binary op-frame `protocol::OpBinary::encode_op`/`decode_op` NOW emit for
# `GltfMutation` — upgraded from the F6-era `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut (18
# standards, gltf among them, were still on this shortcut per the P2-W0 census). `format u8` (the
# repo-wide `store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention byte) + `tag u8` (this variant's own
# ordinal, with frozen tags `NoMutation`=0 .. `SetAnimation`=23 and semantic additions
# `TransformNode`=24, `ReparentNode`=25, `BindNodeMesh`=26, `BindPrimitiveMaterial`=27) are the two
# REAL fixed leading fields, individually, genuinely protocol-walkable — §2.5's recursive/opaque-
# tail pattern for a data-carrying enum whose PAYLOAD shape varies per variant (`Prim::Ref` to a
# nested struct/enum still unconditionally errors at walk time, `protocol-prim-ref-recursion`, and
# `repeat`'s own arms are tag-DISPATCHED, not a bare "N fields of variable per-variant shape"). The
# Rust `encode_op`/`decode_op` side (../🦀️component.rs) IS genuinely, fully structured real binary
# per variant (real varint indices, real per-item recursive encoding via this artifact's own
# `write_bin_*`/`read_bin_*` value codecs, reused verbatim from `../../🔺️diff/🦀️component.rs`'s
# `RealBinary*` regions) — only the PROTOCOL DESCRIPTION stops at the fixed 2-byte header, same
# documented boundary every other hand-rolled `OpBinary` upgrade in this program hits.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
